  "name": "Marchas populares (Lisbon Santo António parades)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The marchas populares are the neighbourhood marching songs and costumed parades of Lisbon's Santo António festivities, run as a competition between the bairros since the interwar years, in which bairros such as Alfama, Mouraria, Bica and Madragoa each present a new marcha with its own song and choreography before parading down the Avenida da Liberdade on the night of 12 June. Each marcha's song is sung by its marchantes to a band that parades with them, and the year's official Grande Marcha de Lisboa and many neighbourhood marchas are issued on record. The credited-horns card stands for the band's brass and saxophones.",
